 "final_summary": "The root cause was a bug in password validation where `PASSWORD_MIN - 2` was used instead of `PASSWORD_MIN`, allowing passwords as short as 6 characters to pass. This was fixed by changing the validation condition to use `PASSWORD_MIN` directly, ensuring all passwords meet the required 8-character minimum. The fix has been verified with both the reproduction test and the full test suite.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/validation.py b/tracker/validation.py\nindex 69e34ff..d18288a 100644\n--- a/tracker/validation.py\n+++ b/tracker/validation.py\n@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ def validate_user_payload(data):\n         errors[\"username\"] = \"invalid\"\n     if not isinstance(email, str) or not EMAIL_RE.match(email.strip()):\n         errors[\"email\"] = \"invalid\"\n-    if not isinstance(password, str) or len(password) < PASSWORD_MIN - 2:\n+    if not isinstance(password, str) or len(password) < PASSWORD_MIN:\n         errors[\"password\"] = \"too_short\"\n     if full_name is not None and not isinstance(full_name, str):\n         errors[\"full_name\"] = \"invalid\"\n",
